			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825876">
									

<p>Thank you for the crit :)</p>
<p>The issue of mundanity is definitely a great point. Originally I was going for a less intensive, purposefully weak object that took a backseat to what an internal investigation within the foundation might look like, and how an organization with zero transparency might carry out, or fail to do that. This has turned out to be a bit of a miss. Either scaling down the story (focusing on the little white lies of bureaucracy with a site manager trying to cover for themselves rather than the top brass) or scaling up the object seems like the way to go.</p>
<p>My plan was, since the foundation never finds out when the object ended up on site, to have the origins remain a mystery, but I see how that could definitely be unsatisfying despite that being the intention.</p>
<p>As for the image, I'm not really sure what I can do to aid that other than attempting to mess around with it in photoshop or something that I've never used before, I do see where you are coming from with that though.</p>
<p>Thanks again so much for the crit and extra pair of eyes on this, you've been a massive help!</p>

