														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825875">
									

<p>There's nothing really to this currently. Weird laptop. Why is it even an anomaly? This could just be a hacker who has an algorithm that will continually release classified documents, etc.</p>
<p><em>More importantly, try to answer the following questions and then edit your post accordingly.</em></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>You get 400 words in the last four sections of the post to expand upon your idea, so I think that you should attempt to explore this further. <strong>This does not mean providing a link to the draft. This is about convincing people that you have a good idea and the ability to sell that good idea.</strong></p>
<p>What are the stakes of this anomaly? - in it's current form, why couldn't the foundation just throw it in a box and forget about it?</p>
<p>What will you do to get the reader to feel invested in these events? Is there someone we can relate to?</p>
<p>What is the narrative journey of the article? Where do we start and then where do we end?</p>
<p>What is the thematic core to your article? What are you trying to say?</p>
</div>
</div>
