			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825851">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The Foundation's researchers are invited to take in a terrible show and rewarded with intelligence at the cost of nightmares.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>A Foundation researcher discovers a letter on their desk, inviting them to join a fellow scholar in taking in a show. The letter comes with a ticket to see &quot;The Ambassador's Strolling Players&quot; and instructions to burn it on a certain time and date.</p>
<p>Under heavy monitoring, the researcher complies and is transported to what appears to be a renaissance era opera house. Once arrived he is greeted by a strange crow man who tells him to stay silent through the performance and meet him back by concessions during the intermission.</p>
<p>The crow man then sits the researcher down in a massive theater filled with other strange creatures. On stage a disturbing show is performed showing a group of masked individuals convincing a strange creature they have its best interests at heart before betraying it in the end.</p>
<p>An intermission is called and the crow man joins the researcher by the concession stand. He says he needs to say as little as possible, and nothing even resembling a name can be used here. He hands the doctor a packet filled with enhanced containment procedures for some of the Foundation's most nasty SCPs.</p>
<p>They watch the conclusion of the play, seeing the &quot;heroes&quot; in masks bringing forth all of the riches they stole from the strange creature before &quot;The Ambassador&quot; who accepts them with a nod, which the masked actors receive with almost orgasmic delight.</p>
<p>Then the crow creature offers the researcher &quot;a lift back&quot; and teleports the researcher back to the test site before leaving.</p>
<p>The containment strategies the crow creature provided prove to be extremely effective in preventing breaches.</p>
<p>Other researchers in the Foundation begin receiving similar messages, inviting them to see other grotesque plays in exchange for valuable intelligence.</p>
<p>This goes on for some time until at one point, a researcher arrives at the opera house to see the actor who played &quot;The Ambassador&quot; in the crow's place. It gives the researcher a box that turns out to contain the crow's head and the researcher arrives back at home.</p>
<p>No further tickets are received.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> &quot;Most likely SCP-XXXX is neutralized, but if you receive a ticket, you are to await an O5 vote before taking further action. Someone out there took a big risk to help us and it cost him everything. We cannot allow it to cost us everything too.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I look forward to your comments!</p>

							</div>

								
					
