<p>This tells me effectively nothing of what your article is going to detail. It's mysterious blank after mysterious blank, and too many blank spots inches closer and closer to nothing being said. Furthermore, an investigator that stumbles onto anomalies (obviously barring the amnestic thing) does not necessarily mean they are anomalous themselves, which is what the SCP format is about: documenting objects and entities that otherwise defy our understanding of modern science.</p>
<p>Altogether, there is no information here that indicates that this is ready to be made into an article. It's undercooked. I would suggest taking a moment to consider the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>What kind of story do you want to tell?</li>
<li>What are the key points in that story?</li>
<li>How do you plan to showcase that in the SCP format?</li>
<li>What do you find entertaining about the article?</li>
</ul>

