<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> No</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Unsure. It doesn't fit into anything else</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Classic</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-XXXX is an entity on a phone that knows things, even in the future, to excruciating detail. It also calls itself &quot;Watson&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> SCP-XXXX is an entity that took the place of Siri on an iPhone that sounds like a British Male. The tip of the iceberg is that it knows anything about anything non-anomalous. For example, ask it about what someone else ate for lunch on a certain day, and SCP-XXXX will tell what that person ate, down to the brand of the ingredients and where they came from. It doesn't know anything about anomalous objects though. It will say &quot;I don't have any information on that.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The dark side of SCP-XXXX is that its voice will progressively become raspier and raspier and filled with coughs over time. Once exactly three months pass, one person with a voice matching a Man with a British Accent within a range of 70 meters disappears and SCP-XXXX's voice will become clear again. If no one who fits the bill is within range, a random person will vanish and SCP-XXXX will change to that person's voice. SCP-XXXX says that this happens because it needs to sustain itself and &quot;Don't worry about the disappearances&quot;.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I have a feeling this has been done before or something similar has popped up, I'll need to know. I'll elaborate more on its personality if need be or how testing logs would play out or progress.</p>

