<p><strong>Seeking Greenlight:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Hook:</strong> A Private Investigator has been seen at multiple (31) instances near newly discovered SCPs. Seems to be unaffected by many SCPs and Amnestics.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Investigator Poz has been very elusive to the foundation and could be used as an asset. He, also, seems to know of SCPs and how to find them. Recently he has been seen to be unaffected by SCP-XXXX (Death-bringer #321) an SCP that predicts deaths. He was also unaffected by SCP-XXXX (Nightshift Hellscape) a place that affects people beyond repair mentally or otherwise. Investigator Poz has not been located as of yet.</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Containment procedures and SCP information first. Then the instances of where he has been sighted.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The Private Investigator known as Investigator Howard Poz has been spotted at multiple sites of SCPs (31 known instances). He is drawn to SCPs for some anomalous reason not yet discovered. The reason the foundation knows this is an anomalous property is because he has found 3 in Russia, 2 in China, 4 in Canada, 12 across the USA, 3 in Brazil etc. Finding one or two is natural, but finding 31 before the foundation is unnatural. He seems to be unaffected by amnestics up to Class C if not more. All the SCPs he has been seen at are newly discovered. The foundation does not know if he is creating the SCPs or just discovering them. If the latter is true he could make a good asset for the foundation. However if the former is true, we need to take immediate action to secure the Investigator.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> SCPs he has been spotted at will be recorded</p>

